---
import AboutHeroImage from '../assets/blog-placeholder-about.jpg';
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About This Site"
	description="Why this blog looks like a lost page from 1999 without inheriting 1999's usability problems."
	pubDate={new Date('August 08 2021')}
	heroImage={AboutHeroImage}
>
	<p>
		This blog is built around a simple constraint: keep the charm of early personal websites without
		bringing back their worst habits. That means loud borders, bright accents, and playful layout
		framing on the outside, with a clean reading column and predictable spacing once you are inside a
		post.
	</p>

	<p>
		Tailwind now drives the entire interface, which makes the visual language more consistent across
		the homepage, archive, and article views. Shared utility patterns handle the retro panels, badge
		elements, and color palette so the theme feels intentional instead of improvised page by page.
	</p>

	<p>
		The palette leans into ocean blues, candy pinks, mint greens, and warm sand backgrounds because
		that combination evokes old homepage aesthetics without reducing legibility. The body copy stays
		in a calmer sans face, while the headings and micro-labels take the louder retro treatment.
	</p>

	<p>
		If you want to personalize it further, the main things to replace are the site title, the home
		page copy, this page’s text, and the placeholder post images. The structure is already set up so
		those edits stay content-focused rather than requiring another round of layout work.
	</p>
</Layout>
